Spain</article-title><source>Electromagnetic Biology and Medicine</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>169</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1081/JBC-120024625</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Santini</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Santini</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Danze</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Le Ruz</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Seigne</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Investigation on the health of people living near mobile telephone relay stations: I/Incidence according to distance and sex</article-title><source>Pathol Biol (Paris)</source><year>2002</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>373</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12168254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moffatt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mulloli</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhopal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Foy</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillimore</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An exploration of awareness bias in two environmental epidemiology studies</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><year>2000</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11021620</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001648-200003000-00020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bornkessel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Schubert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wuschek<